---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<section class="py-10 md:py-16 px-6 relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-[900px] h-[500px] opacity-[0.12]"
         style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center bottom, #d4af37 0%, transparent 65%);"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="continuum-rule max-w-7xl mx-auto absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-full"></div>
  <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-12">
      <div class="glass-card p-6">
        <span class="eyebrow block mb-3" style="color:#89b4fa;">The discipline</span>
        <h3 class="text-[1rem] mb-2">Intent Engineering</h3>
        <p class="text-[0.8125rem] text-text-muted mb-3">
          The category has a founding essay: what the level above the IDE contains, why
          the bottleneck is malformed demand, and what a year of working there taught.
        </p>
        <a href="https://daviguides.github.io/articles/machine-learning/2026/04/25/intent-engineering.html"
           class="text-[0.8125rem] font-mono text-[#89b4fa]">Read the article →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="glass-card p-6">
        <span class="eyebrow block mb-3" style="color:#a6e3a1;">The open door</span>
        <h3 class="text-[1rem] mb-2">Gradients, open source</h3>
        <p class="text-[0.8125rem] text-text-muted mb-3">
          The behavioral standards layer (arché, shodo, kinhin, zazen) is open and already
          in use by other developers. It is the part of Continuum you can run today.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/daviguides" class="text-[0.8125rem] font-mono text-[#a6e3a1]">On GitHub →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="glass-card p-6">
        <span class="eyebrow block mb-3" style="color:#d4af37;">The posture</span>
        <h3 class="text-[1rem] mb-2">Supervision that never stalls</h3>
        <p class="text-[0.8125rem] text-text-muted">
          Autonomy that cannot be inspected is opacity with a better name. Every mode is
          named, every gate is checkable, every session can be reopened by hand, and the
          merge is always yours.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center max-w-[640px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-[1.75rem] md:text-[2.25rem] mb-4">The work continues.<br/>You decide where it matters.</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted text-[0.9375rem] mb-8">
        Continuum is in production daily and being hardened for strangers. If you want
        early access, a pilot, or a conversation about the layer above the editor:
      </p>
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/daviguides/"
         class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-lg text-[0.875rem] font-medium
                bg-[#d4af37] text-crust hover:bg-[#e0c15c] transition-colors">
        Get in touch
      </a>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[0.75rem] italic text-text-muted">
        Works with your existing repo and your existing model subscription. No server, no account.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-text-dim">or write to the studio: Tiphareth Studio</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
